        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Occupying a prime penthouse position in the very centre of Temple Bar, Apartment 11 at 7A Fownes Street Upper presents a rare opportunity to acquire a beautifully finished city home with one of the most sought-after features in Dublin 2 — a substantial private roof terrace. Stylishly presented throughout and offered in true turnkey condition, this is a property that perfectly balances contemporary living with an unrivalled city centre lifestyle.\r\n\r\nThoughtfully designed and finished to a high standard, the apartment boasts bright, well-proportioned accommodation complemented by bespoke fitted cabinetry, quality finishes and excellent use of space throughout. A striking mezzanine level overlooks the main living area, providing exceptional flexibility as a home office, guest space, creative studio or additional reception area, adapting effortlessly as needed.\r\n\r\nThe undisputed highlight is the magnificent private roof terrace. Exceptionally spacious by city centre standards, it offers a tranquil escape above the bustling streets below, creating the perfect setting for outdoor dining, entertaining or simply relaxing while enjoying rooftop views across Dublin. Properties within Temple Bar offering private outdoor space of this scale are exceptionally rare and consistently command significant buyer interest.\r\n\r\nThe bright open-plan living and dining room is ideal for both everyday living and entertaining, while the separate kitchen is well-appointed and highly functional. The generous double bedroom features fitted wardrobes, with the stylish bathroom and plenty of internal storage completing the accommodation. Benefiting from a C-rated BER, the apartment offers an excellent balance of comfort, efficiency and central convenience.\r\n\r\nLocated in the cultural heart of Dublin, residents are surrounded by an unrivalled selection of award-winning restaurants, cafés, galleries, theatres and boutique shopping. Grafton Street, Trinity College, Dublin Castle, St. Stephen's Green, the IFSC and Grand Canal Dock are all within comfortable walking distance, making this an ideal home for , couples or those seeking a premium Dublin base. \r\n\r\nAccommodation \r\nEntrance Hall - 3.8m x 1.9m\r\nLiving Room - 3.9m x 3.3m\r\nDining Area - 3.9m x 1.9m\r\nKitchen - 1.8m x 3.2m\r\nBedroom - 3.9m x 3.2m\r\nBathroom - 1.9m x 1.9m\r\nMezzanine - 3.9m x 2.9m\r\n\r\nLocal area\r\nBus routes (within 10 mins): 9, 13, 15/15A/15B, 16, 27, 39/39A, 49, 54A, 65/65B, 77A, C1-C6, H1-H3, G1 & G2\r\nLuas: Trinity/Westmoreland (Green Line) – c. 5 minutes by foot. Jervis (Red Line) – c. 6 minutes by foot\r\nDart: Tara Street – c. 10 minutes by foot\r\n\r\nProperty features\r\nc. 63 sq. m. (678 sq. ft.)\r\nElectric heating\r\nC3 – BER rating\r\nManagement fees: €2,000 per annum\r\nYear of construction: c. 2000\r\n\r\nFeatures\r\nPenthouse apartment in the heart of Temple Bar \r\nC-rated BER \r\nExceptional turnkey condition throughout \r\nLarge private roof terrace with rooftop city views \r\nFlexible mezzanine level ideal as a home office, guest space or second living area \r\nBespoke fitted cabinetry \r\nBright open-plan living and dining accommodation \r\nExcellent storage"
      },
